On .NET 10, **you no longer need `TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport`**. That property is only required on .NET 9 and earlier to bridge `dotnet test` (VSTest mode) with MTP.

Instead, .NET 10 has native MTP support — just add a `"test"` section to your `global.json`:

```json
{
  "sdk": {
    "version": "10.0.100"
  },
  "test": {
    "runner": "Microsoft.Testing.Platform"
  }
}
```

Then remove `TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport` from your `.csproj`.

**Key difference:** With the native mode, `dotnet test` passes MTP arguments directly (e.g., `dotnet test --report-trx`) — no `--` separator needed.

